cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KineScope: Research Infrastructure for Active Inference of Unfamiliar 3D Mechanisms"
message: "If you use KineScope, please cite this software release and the associated benchmark paper when available."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Jerry Yuze
date-released: 2026-07-28
license: MIT
keywords:
  - multimodal reasoning
  - spatial reasoning
  - system identification
  - active learning
  - twisty puzzles
  - benchmark
  - out-of-distribution generalization
abstract: >-
  KineScope is deterministic research infrastructure for compiling,
  simulating, rendering, and evaluating unfamiliar three-dimensional mechanisms.
  It provides exact twisty-puzzle mechanics, procedural shape modification,
  state-dependent constraints, synchronized observation channels, JSON-first
  benchmark generation, active mechanics-identification oracles, and a stateless
  server API.
